The assert statements are generated based on the comments in the csharp code starting with "@@@". If the method returns a negative number, then the count of elements in the list remains the same. If the method does not return -1, then the count of the list must be greater than zero or the count of the list equals the number of instances of "x". The lastIndexOf of the list equals the returned index "New_Ret" or the number "x". Lastly, the boolean flag for seeing whether the list contains "x" remains the same.--------------------
public static int Sum(int x, int y)
{
    int sum = x + y;
    Debug.Assert(sum >= x && sum >= y);
    return sum;
}
